<Page title="Home">
  <p>Open-source program planning for engineering teams.</p>
  <h1>Plan the work.<br />Respect the capacity.</h1>
  <p>Planacity is being built to help engineering teams structure work, build
    realistic plans, and communicate commitments with Program Management.</p>
  <p class="status"><strong>Early development - Visual Planning in progress.</strong>
    The source preview can create, edit, save, and reopen local Program Plans,
    including JSON backups. Jira CSV mapping, import preview, baseline comparison,
    and CSV export are available. Timeline now offers day, week, and month
    scales, grouping, filters, directional dependency arrows, and bar-edge date resizing.
    No stable packaged download is available yet.</p>
  <h2>The first useful step</h2>
  <p>Create a Program Plan with Epics, Tasks, Subtasks, people, estimates, and dates.
    Save it locally, reopen it, and continue planning. Try the fictional example
    using the <a href="https://github.com/tidus747/planacity/blob/main/docs/getting-started.md">getting-started guide</a>.</p>
  <h2>The longer-term workflow</h2>
  <p>Import -> Plan -> Balance -> Communicate -> Commit</p>
  <p>CSV connects planning with Jira. Future releases will add
    capacity and program communication. Jira remains the execution
    system of record.</p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/tidus747/planacity">Follow development on GitHub</a></p>
</Page>
